DevOps Interview Preparation Series — Kubernetes (K8s) Scenarios 🚀
#DevOps #Kubernetes #K8s

If you’re preparing for a DevOps or Site Reliability Engineer (SRE) interview, you can’t skip Kubernetes (K8s) — the core of modern cloud-native infrastructure.

 Kubernetes questions in interviews often go beyond theory — they test your hands-on troubleshooting, scaling, and automation experience.

Here are real-world Kubernetes scenario-based interview questions you should master 👇

What is Kubernetes and how does it differ from Docker Swarm?
Explain the architecture of Kubernetes — API Server, Controller Manager, Scheduler, etc.
What is a Pod and how is it different from a container?
What are Deployments, ReplicaSets, and StatefulSets — and when would you use each?
How do you perform a rolling update and rollback in Kubernetes?
Your pod is stuck in “CrashLoopBackOff” — how do you troubleshoot it?
How do you check which pod is consuming the most CPU or memory?
Explain the difference between readiness and liveness probes.
How can you restart a specific pod or deployment in Kubernetes?
How do you expose an application running inside a pod to the outside world?
What are the different types of Kubernetes services (ClusterIP, NodePort, LoadBalancer)?
How do you secure communication between pods and services in Kubernetes?
Explain the concept of ConfigMaps and Secrets — and how you’d use them.
How can you perform zero-downtime deployment in Kubernetes?
Your application is not resolving environment variables — what could be the issue?
How do you use taints and tolerations in Kubernetes scheduling?
What’s the difference between a DaemonSet and a Deployment?
How do you restrict certain pods from communicating with others?
Explain how Ingress works in Kubernetes.
How can you perform a health check of pods and nodes using Bash or kubectl commands?
How do you monitor Kubernetes clusters using Prometheus and Grafana?
What are Init containers and when do you use them?
How do you roll back to a previous Deployment version in Kubernetes?
Explain what happens when you run kubectl apply -f deployment.yaml.
How do you handle “ImagePullBackOff” or “OOMKilled” errors?
What are Kubernetes Namespaces and why are they important?
How do you integrate Kubernetes with Jenkins or GitHub Actions in a CI/CD pipeline?
How do you implement pod auto-scaling in Kubernetes?
How do you back up and restore your Kubernetes cluster and resources?
What are some best practices for securing Kubernetes clusters in production?

Pro Tip:
Kubernetes mastery is not about memorizing commands — it’s about understanding how components interact.
 Focus on:
 ✅ Troubleshooting (kubectl describe, kubectl logs)
 ✅ Health checks and monitoring
 ✅ Deployment strategies (Blue-Green, Canary)
 ✅ Security (RBAC, Network Policies)
